# Upstream reference checkouts — ~113 MB, with nested .git directories.
# Never committed: reproducible from the commit SHAs recorded in PROVENANCE.md.
#
# THREE directories, not two. PROVENANCE.md section 7 registers all three, and
# `ref-quarantine` fails the build when the register and the disk disagree — so a clone
# that restores only the first two goes red. The third is a commercial specimen: park it,
# never build it, never read it (section 3).
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch 21.1.9 git@github.com:primefaces/primeng.git ref/primeng
#   git clone --depth 1 git@github.com:primefaces/primeuix.git ref/primeuix
#   # ref/primeng.dev — see PROVENANCE.md section 7 for the command and its two traps
ref/

# Maintainer working notes. Never published.
.agl/

node_modules/
dist/
.angular/
*.log
.DS_Store
pnpm-lock.yaml.bak
# E2E evidence screenshots — regenerable, no binaries in the tree
test-results/
# Playwright MCP scratch output (snapshots, console logs, screenshots) — same rule
.playwright-mcp/
# Serena MCP project config and symbol cache — 48 MB of regenerable .pkl. Serena intends its
# project.yml to be versioned, but this repo already keeps maintainer tooling out of the public
# tree (`.agl/` above), and committing it would impose a particular AI tool on contributors.
.serena/

# Provenance tarballs: kept locally / in a private evidence store, never published.
# primeng-21.1.9.tgz ships proprietary "PRIMENG LTS VERSIONS LICENSE" text inside its
# LICENSE.md. provenance/manifest.json holds the SHA-256 checksums — that is the proof.
# Reproduce: node tools/provenance/archive-mit.mjs && node tools/provenance/archive-mit.mjs --verify
provenance/tarballs/

# Build output of the forked primeuix packages (tsup)
packages/angulux-*/dist/
plans/

# Internal specifications. `tools/check-public-tree.mjs` already REFUSES these in the index;
# this keeps them from ever being staged in the first place, the same way `plans/` is handled.
docs/specs/

# Local secrets — npm publish tokens etc. Never committed. A bypass-2FA token
# lived here during the BL-11 publish; keep it out of the index for good.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated LLM-facing site, built from the committed corpus by the Pages workflow.
site/

# Showcase payloads: the API sliced out of the committed corpus, and the demo code extracted
# from the committed demo files. Both derive from tracked sources and are rebuilt by the
# app's own prebuild step — committing them would create a second copy that can go stale
# without anything noticing, which is the exact failure the extraction exists to prevent.
apps/showcase/public/
